  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The half granny works in rows rather than rounds, giving a triangular motif that fills the perimeter gaps of a granny square blanket without cutting any full squares. Unlike a square motif, it has one straight base edge to align with the blanket border and two diagonal sides that match the angle of adjacent granny corners. Three rows produce a triangle the same height as half a standard four-round granny square."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 14 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, blocking mat and pins."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3 rows in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 10 cm wide, 5 cm tall. This matches the profile of the outer edge gap in a blanket of standard four-round granny squares."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
