        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: ch 3 at the start of each row counts as the first "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "tr"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout. Work is turned at the end of each row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 4. Work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) all into the 4th ch from hook. This creates the single centre corner. Turn. (6 tr, 1 ch-2 corner.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 3 tr into the ch-2 corner space. Ch 2. Work 3 more tr into the same ch-2 corner space. Ch 1. Work 3 tr into the space at the end of the row (between the last cluster and the turning chain). Turn. (9 tr, 1 ch-2 corner sp, 1 ch-1 sp.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 3 tr into the first ch-1 space. Ch 1. Work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into the ch-2 corner space. Ch 1. Work 3 tr into the last space at the end of the row. Fasten off. (12 tr, 1 ch-2 corner sp, 2 ch-1 sps.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-half-granny"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Block"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flat by pinning the straight base edge and the two diagonal sides. The ch-2 corner at the top pins to a right angle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew the two diagonal sides of the half granny to the outer edges of adjacent full granny squares using a whip stitch or mattress stitch. The ch-1 spaces along the sides align with the corresponding spaces on the full squares."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 °C or hand wash. Lay flat to dry. Block again if seams pull the triangle out of shape after washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Once the half granny is comfortable, work the same flat-row principle in reverse: start with a wide foundation chain and decrease to a point to make a quarter granny triangle for corner fills. The lace square motif uses the same granny structure as a base but opens the sides with chain arches."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
